  "query_preview": "..\nRemnants of 93W, now a slowly-rotating trough axis, is expected to\ncontinue bringing scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms\novernight. Then, gradual improvement is expected through Wednesday \nnight as light diffusive southerlies ensue thereafter. As Typhoon \nDolphin (12W) continues to strengthen and pass well northeast of the \nregion, this will induce a much stronger monsoonal flow across the \nMarianas, likely to bring another period of elevated showers and much\nstronger winds by next week.",
